<tbx style="dca" type="TBX-Basic" xml:lang="en" xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:30042:ed-2">
  <tbxHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <source>https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0111</source>
    </fileDesc>
  </tbxHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <conceptEntry id="dpp-0111">
      <languageSection xml:lang="eng">
          <descrip type="definition">
            <p>defined characteristic suitable for the description and differentiation of products or components</p>
          </descrip>
          <note type="note">The concept of type and instance applies to properties.</note>
          <note type="note">This definition applies to properties as described in IEC 61360/ ISO 13584-42.</note>
          <note type="note">The property types are defined in dictionaries (like IEC component data dictionary or ECLASS), they do not have a value. The property type is also called data element type in some standards.</note>
          <note type="note">The property instances have a value and are provided by the manufacturers. A property instance is also called property-value pair in certain standards.</note>
          <note type="note">Properties include nominal value, actual value, runtime variables, measurement values, etc.</note>
          <note type="note">A property describes one characteristic of a given object.</note>
          <note type="note">The specification of a property can include predefined choices of values.</note>
          <ref>IDTA-01001-3.2:2026 (Specification of the Asset Administration Shell — Part 1: Metamodel) 1.1.18</ref>
          <ref>ISO/IEC Guide 77-2; Glossary Industrie 4.0</ref>
      </languageSection>
      </conceptEntry>
    </body>
  </text>
</tbx>
